<html lang="en">
<head>
    <title>Attribute Contribution</title>
    <style>
        h3 { ${REGULAR_LARGE_FONT_STYLE} }
        body { ${REGULAR_FONT_STYLE} }
        code { ${MONOSPACE_FONT_STYLE} }
        h3 code { font-size: inherit; }
        p { margin-top: 0; }
    </style>
</head>
<body style="width: 300px">
    <h3>Attribute Contribution</h3>
    <p><strong>DBN calculation · model-level</strong></p>
    <p>Oracle's <code>PREDICTION_DETAILS</code> returns a signed influence weight for each attribute in each test-row prediction of <em>this trained model</em>. DBN averages the absolute weights for each attribute across the test set.</p>
    <p>Higher values mean stronger influence, whether an attribute supported or opposed the predicted outcome. This is not a percentage, has no fixed maximum, and does not mean that an attribute is positive or desirable.</p>
    <p>Unlike Attribute Importance, this is DBN's summary of Oracle's per-row explanations for this model. Oracle does not return this average directly.</p>
</body>
</html>
